"Nevertheless, crises have a remarkable way of exposing the illusion of absolute self-sufficiency. During the severe winter blackouts that struck the northern region last year, thousands of residents were left without heating or electricity for nearly a week. Initially, panic led to hoarding at local supermarkets. Yet, within forty-eight hours, an extraordinary wave of grassroots solidarity emerged: neighbors opened their homes to the elderly, volunteers organized communal kitchens, and strangers shared generators without expecting compensation.",
