"Proponents of industrial automation emphasize its undeniable benefits for productivity and workplace safety. Machines can operate tirelessly twenty-four hours a day without fatigue, while relieving human laborers from hazardous, physically grueling tasks such as heavy lifting or chemical handling. Furthermore, lower production costs can translate into more affordable consumer goods and enhanced global competitiveness.",
