"Nevertheless, equating internet access with universal access to knowledge overlooks persistent structural inequalities. According to international telecommunications reports, roughly a third of the global population remains offline, predominantly in rural and low-income regions. Even among connected populations, the 'digital divide' persists through unequal bandwidth speeds, prohibitively expensive mobile data plans, and a lack of computer hardware.",
